WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Nature and Character of a Defect Opportunity

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome to this segment on Six Sigma.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.266
We’re going to look at a very interesting concept.

4
00:00:11.266 --> 00:00:14.799
It's been a lot of controversy for a long time

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.800
and that's the idea of defect opportunities.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:28.466
So, what is a defect opportunity? Well it’s really pretty simple.

7
00:00:28.466 --> 00:00:32.466
I think a lot of people over the years have made a big deal out of it.

8
00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:35.732
We even went through in the early 90's through Texas Instruments,

9
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:38.833
at their defense group, called the opportunity wars.

10
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:42.833
It got that bitter, over what constitutes a defect opportunity.

11
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:49.699
Well, after many years of frustrating debate. That was good debate. Healthy debate.

12
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:56.166
We finally come to realize that a defect opportunity is nothing more

13
00:00:56.166 --> 00:01:00.166
than anything you measure

14
00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:04.166
and report

15
00:01:04.166 --> 00:01:10.399
on a regular basis. That's a defect opportunity. So, let me say this.

16
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.633
If I had a little product here, a little widget gizmo, could be a radio

17
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:20.866
or I could have a process, consider that the product.

18
00:01:20.866 --> 00:01:27.832
Like a masseuse has a service process. A massage, you experience the process.

19
00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:33.833
This is a piece of hardware. I could look at a legal defense from a legal point of view.

20
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:38.433
Anything. Whatever that may be.  It’s full of opportunities.

21
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:43.199
So, let's take something that's important to us that we value.

22
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:49.766
If we measure it and report it, then that's a defect opportunity. That simple.

23
00:01:49.766 --> 00:01:55.032
Now, what we’re going to do is look at this in a little greater detail.

24
00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.933
But fundamentally a defect opportunity, an opportunity,

25
00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:05.066
is a set of conditions that is favorable to an end.

26
00:02:05.066 --> 00:02:12.066
Think of that. It's a set of conditions,

27
00:02:12.066 --> 00:02:16.832
that is favorable

28
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:20.199
to some end.

29
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:27.233
Now in this case, the end we’re talking about is a defect.

30
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:33.266
A defect. So, a set of conditions favorable to some end.

31
00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:37.099
Or a defect. Well, let's take a look at it.

32
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:43.466
We’re going to break this down and understand this concept of a defect opportunity.

33
00:02:43.466 --> 00:02:49.899
Condition is a standard. If I have an upper spec limit and a lower spec limit,

34
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:56.866
I have a standard. That's a condition. Think about it.

35
00:02:56.866 --> 00:03:02.466
If I had activity and I had no standard to gauge my activity against.

36
00:03:02.466 --> 00:03:06.499
There can never be a defect, if that's gone.

37
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:13.566
Then I also need now, a process capability.

38
00:03:13.566 --> 00:03:17.566
If there is no process capability,

39
00:03:17.566 --> 00:03:21.032
then all there is, is a potential opportunity, see.

40
00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:26.033
That design specification is a potential opportunity.

41
00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:31.299
If there is a distribution of capability but no design specification,

42
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:37.066
there's potential opportunity. But when that design.

43
00:03:37.066 --> 00:03:40.932
When that process capability is interfaced

44
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:46.199
with the design opportunity, then we have a defect opportunity.

45
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:53.200
Now, let’s think about that for second. I’m going to blow this up again, even larger.

46
00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:00.200
For our discussion here. Here again is that upper spec.

47
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.400
Here is that lower spec. And,

48
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:10.766
here is the process distribution.

49
00:04:10.766 --> 00:04:14.866
Remember, it takes both to be present.

50
00:04:14.866 --> 00:04:21.866
Upper. I’ll just draw that across there real nice, so we can see that.

51
00:04:21.866 --> 00:04:27.099
Now, this region right here in the red.

52
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.700
This is the probability of a defect.

53
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:38.366
That's the probability of a defect. Everything in the green here,

54
00:04:38.366 --> 00:04:44.066
is the probability of yield, or what's good.

55
00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:49.299
This is what's good, that's in the green. Now,

56
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.266
if I don't have a process capability. There's no probability of defects.

57
00:04:54.266 --> 00:05:00.066
If I don't have a standard, then there's nothing to declare these as red.

58
00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:04.166
There’s no reference point, high watermark, to declare them as red.

59
00:05:04.166 --> 00:05:10.332
So, everything would be green. Only when I interface my process

60
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:16.099
with my design, do I have probability of defect.

61
00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:21.433
If there is no interface, guess what?

62
00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:25.199
There is no probability.

63
00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:32.200
So, you can't have a defect. If there's no probability for a defect.

64
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.933
Therefore, to have a defect opportunity,

65
00:05:36.933 --> 00:05:43.966
then the probability of a defect must be greater than zero.

66
00:05:43.966 --> 00:05:50.599
Now, think about that. If there's no distribution, no capability, there's no probability.

67
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:57.600
Probability of defect is zero. If there's a distribution but no standards,

68
00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.766
probability is zero.

69
00:06:00.766 --> 00:06:06.866
Only, when I marry the process

70
00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:14.432
to the design. Does the idea of probability

71
00:06:14.433 --> 00:06:21.099
come into being. Once it comes into being. If the probability is greater than zero,

72
00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:28.100
then there is an opportunity for

73
00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:34.033
defect, that simple. Thus, we have the idea

74
00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:39.599
of probability of defect or defect opportunity.

75
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.600
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
